 "title": "Climate Types and El Niño",
 "emoji": "🌡️",
 "cards": [
  {
   "tag": "Why this matters",
   "h": "Climate is not just weather",
   "b": "<p><b>Weather</b> is what happens today. <b>Climate</b> is the average over about 30 years. Classifying climates gives a language for vegetation, farming and settlement. <b>El Nino</b> explains why some monsoons fail. Both are everyday GS I questions.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Core idea",
   "h": "Koppen's scheme",
   "b": "<svg class=\"d\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 188\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"6\" width=\"55\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f1e4c6\" stroke=\"#a8792a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"37.5\" y=\"23\" fill=\"#7d5a1c\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Letter</text><rect x=\"65\" y=\"6\" width=\"140\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f1e4c6\" stroke=\"#a8792a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"135.0\" y=\"23\" fill=\"#7d5a1c\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Type</text><rect x=\"205\" y=\"6\" width=\"105\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f1e4c6\" stroke=\"#a8792a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"257.5\" y=\"23\" fill=\"#7d5a1c\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Example</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"32\" width=\"55\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"37.5\" y=\"51\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">A</text><rect x=\"65\" y=\"32\" width=\"140\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"135.0\" y=\"51\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tropical, hot all year</text><rect x=\"205\" y=\"32\" width=\"105\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"257.5\" y=\"51\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Congo, Kerala</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"62\" width=\"55\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"37.5\" y=\"81\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">B</text><rect x=\"65\" y=\"62\" width=\"140\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"135.0\" y=\"81\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dry (BW desert, BS steppe)</text><rect x=\"205\" y=\"62\" width=\"105\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"257.5\" y=\"81\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sahara, Thar</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"92\" width=\"55\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"37.5\" y=\"111\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">C</text><rect x=\"65\" y=\"92\" width=\"140\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"135.0\" y=\"111\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Warm temperate</text><rect x=\"205\" y=\"92\" width=\"105\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"257.5\" y=\"111\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mediterranean, N. India</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"122\" width=\"55\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"37.5\" y=\"141\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">D</text><rect x=\"65\" y=\"122\" width=\"140\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"135.0\" y=\"141\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cold snowy forest</text><rect x=\"205\" y=\"122\" width=\"105\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"257.5\" y=\"141\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Siberia, Canada</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"152\" width=\"55\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"37.5\" y=\"171\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">E</text><rect x=\"65\" y=\"152\" width=\"140\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"135.0\" y=\"171\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Polar (ET tundra)</text><rect x=\"205\" y=\"152\" width=\"105\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"257.5\" y=\"171\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Arctic, Himalaya peaks</text></svg><p><b>Wladimir Koppen</b> (first version 1884, revised 1918 and 1936) used temperature, rainfall and natural vegetation. Small letters add detail: <b>f</b> wet all year, <b>w</b> dry winter, <b>s</b> dry summer, <b>h</b> hot, <b>k</b> cold. Highland climates are labelled H.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Core idea",
   "h": "Tropical climates: A",
   "b": "<p><b>Af</b> equatorial: rain every day, dense forest (Amazon, Congo). <b>Am</b> monsoon: short dry spell (Kerala, Bangladesh). <b>Aw</b> savanna: dry winter, grass and scattered trees (Sudan, Brazilian campos, most of peninsular India).</p><p>Annual temperature range is small near the equator; diurnal range is bigger than annual range.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Core idea",
   "h": "Dry and temperate climates: B and C",
   "b": "<p><b>BWh</b> hot desert (Sahara, Thar) at about 30 degrees on west coasts where cold currents add dryness. <b>BS</b> steppe is the grassy fringe.</p><p><b>Cs</b> Mediterranean: wet winters, dry summers (California, Chile, Cape). <b>Cfa</b> China type: humid subtropical. <b>Cfb</b> British type: mild, rain all year, on west coasts at 40-60 degrees.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Core idea",
   "h": "Cold and polar: D and E",
   "b": "<p><b>Df</b> cold with year-round precipitation: Siberia and Canada, the coniferous <b>taiga</b>. Winter is very long and the annual range of temperature is the largest on Earth. <b>ET</b> tundra and <b>EF</b> ice cap. Permafrost thaw is now a climate worry.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Core idea",
   "h": "El Nino and the Walker circulation",
   "b": "<svg class=\"d\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 190\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"6\" width=\"300\" height=\"76\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#dceaec\" stroke=\"#2f6f7a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"24\" fill=\"#2f6f7a\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Normal year (Walker circulation)</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"50\" fill=\"#5d6474\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">East Pacific</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"64\" fill=\"#5d6474\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">cold, high pressure</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"50\" fill=\"#5d6474\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">West Pacific</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"64\" fill=\"#5d6474\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">warm, low, rain</text><line x1=\"80\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"235\" y2=\"40\" stroke=\"#2f6f7a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"38\" fill=\"#2f6f7a\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">trade winds blow west</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"96\" width=\"300\" height=\"86\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f4dcd5\" stroke=\"#a3362a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"114\" fill=\"#a3362a\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">El Nino year</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"140\" fill=\"#5d6474\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">East Pacific</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"154\" fill=\"#5d6474\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">warm, rain, Peru floods</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"140\" fill=\"#5d6474\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">West Pacific</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"154\" fill=\"#5d6474\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">cool, dry, drought</text><line x1=\"235\" y1=\"128\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"128\" stroke=\"#a3362a\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"126\" fill=\"#a3362a\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">trades weaken or reverse</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"174\" fill=\"#5d6474\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Warm water and rain shift east.</text></svg><p><b>El Nino</b> is unusual warming of the central and eastern Pacific, first noticed off Peru near Christmas (el nino means the boy child). The paired atmospheric change is the Southern Oscillation, so together they are <b>ENSO</b>.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Core idea",
   "h": "ENSO and the Indian Ocean Dipole",
   "b": "<svg class=\"d\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 144\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"6\" width=\"75\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f4dcd5\" stroke=\"#a3362a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"47.5\" y=\"30.0\" fill=\"#a3362a\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">El Nino</text><rect x=\"91\" y=\"6\" width=\"219\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"200.5\" y=\"30.0\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Warm phase, SOI negative, every 2-7 years</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"52\" width=\"75\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#dceaec\" stroke=\"#2f6f7a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"47.5\" y=\"76.0\" fill=\"#2f6f7a\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">La Nina</text><rect x=\"91\" y=\"52\" width=\"219\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"200.5\" y=\"76.0\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cool phase, stronger trades, good for monsoon</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"98\" width=\"75\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f1e4c6\" stroke=\"#a8792a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"47.5\" y=\"122.0\" fill=\"#7d5a1c\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">IOD</text><rect x=\"91\" y=\"98\" width=\"219\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"200.5\" y=\"122.0\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Positive: warm west Indian Ocean, aids monsoon</text></svg><p><b>La Nina</b> brings the reverse. India's monsoon is often weak in El Nino years (2002, 2009, 2014, 2015) but not always: 1997 was normal. A positive <b>IOD</b> can offset El Nino, as in 2019 with a strong positive IOD.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Debate",
   "h": "Is climate prediction a gamble?",
   "b": "<p>ENSO is now forecast months ahead, helping farmers and the government stock grain. But the link to India is not one-to-one, because the IOD, the Madden-Julian Oscillation and Eurasian snow also matter. Some studies suggest climate change makes ENSO extremes stronger. Treat claims with care.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Indian angle",
   "h": "India's climates and El Nino",
   "b": "<p>Koppen's map for India: Am (Malabar), Aw (peninsula), BShw (semi-arid Deccan rain shadow), BWhw (Thar), Cwg (Gangetic plain), Dfc (Arunachal), and E (high Himalaya).</p><p>Years like <b>2015</b> and <b>2023</b> (El Nino) brought below-normal rain; 2023 monsoon was about 94% of the long-period average. IMD now uses <b>Mission Mausam</b> (approved 2024) to improve forecasts.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Exam lens",
   "cls": "exam",
   "h": "How to write this",
   "b": "<div class=\"box\"><h4>Likely questions</h4><p>\"Describe the characteristics and distribution of the Mediterranean climate.\" (10 marks)</p><p>\"What is El Nino? How does it affect the Indian monsoon?\" (10 marks)</p></div><p><b>Structure:</b> define; explain the normal Walker cell; show the break; list global effects; then India (monsoon, crops, prices, policy response).</p><p><b>Prelims tip:</b> Mediterranean = west coasts at 30-45 degrees; Peru's coast is where El Nino was first noticed; positive IOD aids the monsoon.</p>"
  }
 ],
